---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-04-founders-sms-consent-v2.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-04',
  title: 'Founders text message consent discloses frequency and HELP, and links the SMS Terms',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'lead-capture', 'sms', 'legal'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 4, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    The optional text message consent on the Founders application at
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> now reads:
    "I agree to receive text messages from BreederHQ about my Founders program application.
    Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help or STOP to opt
    out." A line beneath it links the
    <a href="/legal/sms-terms" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">SMS Terms</a> and
    <a href="/legal/sms-terms#sms-privacy" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">SMS Privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Carriers require toll-free SMS opt-in wording to disclose message frequency and HELP
      instructions and to link the program's terms and privacy notice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The checkbox now submits consent version <code>founders-sms-v2</code>, whose wording the
      platform holds and matches the sentence on screen exactly. The links sit outside that
      sentence and open in a new tab so the form is not lost. The box remains optional and
      unchecked by default.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
